error: `receive` on a channel holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_channel_receive_async.sg:3:17
 3 |     return jobs.receive() ?? 0
   |                 ^^^^^^^
  hint: `await jobs.receiveAsync()` does the same work without holding the thread
